{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/they-came-from/beneath-the-sea/1463595-they-came-from-the-north-pole","id":1463595,"title":"They Came from the North Pole!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","They Came From...","...Beneath the Sea!"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-12T09:05:49-07:00","id":1463595,"title":"They Came from the North Pole!","content":"Hey folks! I'm writing this thread to let you know I'm currently working on a <b>They Came from Beneath the Sea! </b>supplement for the the StoryPath Nexus called <b>They Came from the North Pole!</b>, meant to introduce the tools to have your very own Christmas Special into your games.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar192_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"192\" data-vbnamecard=\"192\">Yossarian</a> , who accepted to be my partner in crime for this endeavour and has far more experience than me with the SP Nexus and the ST Vault, wisely advised me to make a little thread about the project in the forums in order to draw a little attention.<br /> <br /> The supplement itself is at a good stage. We aim to release it in December (which would be fitting), so here's a hint of what you can expect to find in it:<br /> <br /> \u2022 A discussion on how to create a festive game of your own, either as part of your They Came from Beneath the Sea! chronicles or as a merry one-shot.<br /> <br /> \u2022 20 Jolly Cinematics, meant to replicate and endorse the tropes of corny Christmas movies and holiday-adjacent films of all sorts.<br /> <br /> \u2022 18 write-ups of monsters and potential allies, from big names like Santa &amp; Krampus, to creatures like the Gingebread People and the Snowmen. Plus many more!<br /> <br /> I'll leave you here with a small preview of a Special Rule that I know shows the mood well.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> &quot;<b>Got your nose: </b>Should a character steal a snowman\u2019s carrot nose, the poor being suffers from level 3 Complication all rolls until they get their vegetable appendage back, while other snowmen present in the scene as the crime happens gain the Panicked Condition. The Attitude of all snowmen against the character and their companions starts at \u201cNegative Attitude 4\u201d for the remainder of the story, since the group has proven to be a hated enemy of all snowmankind.&quot; </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> If you think this book could be up your alley, keep an eye on this thread and the SP Nexus itself!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 10-14-2021, 01:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T11:00:15-07:00","id":1463601,"title":"","content":"I'm all for the <b>They Came From!</b> supplement for the Christmas festivity. <a href=\"https://emojipedia.org/christmas-tree/\" target=\"_blank\">\ud83c\udf84</a> <a href=\"https://emojipedia.org/santa-claus/\" target=\"_blank\">\ud83c\udf85</a> <a href=\"https://emojipedia.org/deer/\" target=\"_blank\">\ud83e\udd8c</a><br /> <br /> BUT why <b>Beneath the Sea</b>? Not more logical would be using <b>Beyond the Grave</b> engine? \ud83e\udd14<br /> <br /> As I suppose Krampus will be slasher type villain of many 'dark christmas' movies... And Slashers are in the <b>Murder Lake</b> supplement for <b>Beyond the Grave</b> added...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-12-2021, 02:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T11:16:26-07:00","id":1463602,"title":"","content":"Only Beneath the Sea! is currently available for the SP Nexus, so it's not possible to use other They Came From games or make reference to them for now.<br /> <br /> Besides, the core engine doesn't change. Given we also provide our own Cinematics and monsters, Beneath the Sea! works perfectly.<br /> <br /> Our Krampus...is not what you have in mind \ud83d\ude1b <br /> <br /> Though, even if that were the case, it's not like you need Beyond the Grave! for a murderous villain!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 10-12-2021, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T19:58:26-07:00","id":1463642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/they-came-from/beneath-the-sea/1463595-they-came-from-the-north-pole#post1463595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey folks! I'm writing this thread to let you know I'm currently working on a <b>They Came from Beneath the Sea! </b>supplement for the the StoryPath Nexus called <b>They Came from the North Pole!</b>, meant to introduce the tools to have your very own Christmas Special into your games.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar192_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"192\" data-vbnamecard=\"192\">Yossarian</a> , who accepted to be my partner in crime for this endeavour and has far more experience than me with the SP Nexus and the ST Vault, wisely advised me to make a little thread about the project in the forums in order to draw a little attention.<br /> <br /> The supplement itself is at a good stage. We aim to release it in December (which would be fitting), so here's a hint of what you can expect to find in it:<br /> <br /> \u2022 A discussion on how to create a festive game of your own, either as part of your They Came from Beneath the Sea! chronicles or as a merry one-shot.<br /> <br /> \u2022 19 Jolly Cinematics, meant to replicate and endorse the tropes of corny Christmas movies and holiday-adjacent films of all sorts.<br /> <br /> \u2022 18 write-ups of monsters and potential allies, from big names like Santa &amp; Krampus, to creatures like the Gingebread People and the Snowmen. Plus many more!<br /> <br /> I'll leave you here with a small preview of a Special Rule that I know shows the mood well.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> &quot;<b>Got your nose: </b>Should a character steal a snowman\u2019s carrot nose, the poor being suffers from level 3 Complication all rolls until they get their vegetable appendage back, while other snowmen present in the scene as the crime happens gain the Panicked Condition. The Attitude of all snowmen against the character and their companions starts at \u201cNegative Attitude 4\u201d for the remainder of the story, since the group has proven to be a hated enemy of all snowmankind.&quot; </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> If you think this book could be up your alley, keep an eye on this thread and the SP Nexus itself!</div> </div> </div> </div>I fully endorse this supplement, which is going to be amazing, but I also want it known that I completely denounce all of the puns within it, even the ones I helped come up with.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T20:28:17-07:00","id":1463643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/they-came-from/beneath-the-sea/1463595-they-came-from-the-north-pole?p=1463602#post1463602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides, the core engine doesn't change. Given we also provide our own Cinematics and monsters, Beneath the Sea! works perfectly.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are small difference between Beneath the Sea! and Beyond the Grave! mechanics, for example on Scale counting. ( Based on KS backer version.) But, I suppose, they are negligible in larger suplement...<br /> <br /> If Beyond the Grave! have premier before North Pole!, you plan to make some rules add on, if something comes up in conflict with Beyond the Grave!?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T20:39:10-07:00","id":1463644,"title":"","content":"I advise you to promote North Pole! on They Came From... RPGs gamelines Facebook group, on premiere! \ud83d\ude0e <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/groups/916327439281166\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.facebook.com/groups/916327439281166</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T22:11:54-07:00","id":1463649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/they-came-from/beneath-the-sea/1463595-they-came-from-the-north-pole?p=1463644#post1463644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I advise you to promote North Pole! on They Came From... RPGs gamelines Facebook group, on premiere! \ud83d\ude0e <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/groups/916327439281166\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.facebook.com/groups/916327439281166</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I think the professional writer/developer knows how to pimp their product, Hamster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T00:53:45-07:00","id":1463662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/they-came-from/beneath-the-sea/1463595-they-came-from-the-north-pole?p=1463643#post1463643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are small difference between Beneath the Sea! and Beyond the Grave! mechanics, for example on Scale counting. ( Based on KS backer version.) But, I suppose, they are negligible in larger suplement...<br /> <br /> If Beyond the Grave! have premier before North Pole!, you plan to make some rules add on, if something comes up in conflict with Beyond the Grave!?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehm, no. The way Scale works doesn't change, because why should it? The &quot;differences&quot; you mention are, at best, how certain sections of the System chapter are phrased or the fluff within.<br /> <br /> The core mechanics of the They Came From games don't change. There's nothing to suppose, nor conflicts to expect.<br /> <br /> What we may consider doing is small alterations in the future to take in account other games when they become available for the Nexus. Though that's something for a distant day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 10-13-2021, 04:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T03:55:58-07:00","id":1463686,"title":"","content":"The only difference in rules terms between Sea and Grave is when dealing with PCs developing supernatural powers. BTS uses the idea of Encountered while BTG uses the Haunted, and the rules a re a bit different (not much though).<br /> <br /> Also, my first reading of the title the first thing that come to my mind was The Thing, and it\u2019s pretty much BTS essentially.<br /> <br /> Thematically, any series can (and very often will) have the Xmas special, no matter if dealing with shrimp people or zombies, so both are great options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T10:44:11-07:00","id":1463853,"title":"","content":"Update: the Cinematics are going to be 20, because 19 is an ugly number to have.<br /> <br /> Here's the fiction from one as appetizer:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <i>As the hissing gears of his LandWalk suit resonated in the snowy silence of Christmas Eve, Finnius McFlipper III, commander of the Prefecture of the Pod\u2019s forces assigned to the North Pole operations, advanced through the crab people\u2019s ranks. Though he made sure to leave a row of crustacean soldiers between him and the gathered enemies, the evil dolphin couldn\u2019t resist to gloat.</i><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cYou three have been a thorn in my side for far too long\u201d The commander waved his fin around at a slow yet dramatic pace, a calculated effort to instill fear in his foes. In front him, Scirocco, Peggy, and Antonio had nowhere to go, dozens of enemies surrounding them. \u201cBut it was only a matter of time. Santa can\u2019t help you anymore and you\u2019re finally trapped. I am victorious. Now hand me the Orb of the Longest Night and I\u2019ll consider granting you a quick demise\u201d.</i><br /> <br /> <i>The three friends looked at each other. They hugged for a few precious instants, then Antonio made a step forward. He made a gesture with his arms Finnius didn\u2019t recognize but whose vulgar intent was far too clear, and said \u201cSuck it, fish. I\u2019m not going down without a fight\u201d.</i><br /> <br /> <i>The dolphin despot\u2019s eyes narrowed. \u201cVery well, I\u2019m going to enjoy this\u201d. Finnius pressed a button, sending his mechanical legs into battle mode. \u201cKill them all!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <i>The crab people ducked, grabbing enough snow in their claws to make a satisfying snowball. The humans responded in kind. The stillness of the night broke, as screams, fake missile noises, and accusations of pretending to not having being hit filled the air.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Snowball war. Snowball war never changes.</i><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 10-14-2021, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T12:37:05-07:00","id":1464215,"title":"","content":"Consider me enthused!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T11:02:08-07:00","id":1465790,"title":"","content":"Things proceed well! The text is finished and a December release seems likely indeed!<br /> <br /> More updates will follow as Christmas approaches, but odds are this supplement will appear under your tree as we hoped it would.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T04:55:40-08:00","id":1467429,"title":"","content":"Alright, as promised, it's time for a preview.<br /> <br /> I've picked the Snowmen as a good example of what you can be find in our book. They're a classic and fit the mood well, though some more unexpected creatures will make an appearance as well. When it comes to previews, though, I feel like snowmen are a perfect pick.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Snowmen</b><br /> \u201cLook buddy, leave the driveway as is, keep your paws off my buttons, and we won\u2019t have no problem.\u201d<br /> \u2014 Snowman Barney<br /> <br /> Arguably the largest animated wonders roaming the festive nights (aside from the occasional living tree or giant Santa statue), snowmen are exactly the humanoid piles of snow their name describes.<br /> <br /> A mere anthropomorphic shape isn\u2019t enough for such a being to acquire life. Rather, a proper snowperson needs, at the very least, an array of items to represent its eyes and arms, plus some articles of clothing to provide the necessary dignity. Snowpeople insist a carrot nose is the most essential feature of all, though their ability to survive even when the carrot\u2019s removed \u2014 the most heinous crime snowkind can conceive \u2014 suggests this is simply superstition.<br /> <br /> Despite the more common term, snowmen, snowwomen, and snowpeople of all genders exist, with the exact distinction based more around how the snowperson perceives themself.<br /> <br /> Given that they often arise through sheer happenstance, or by the command of a more powerful festive beings, snowmen aren\u2019t always blessed with free will, but are rather bound by byzantine magical laws to follow their instinctual directives. Even those snowmen with total control over their actions tend to gather together, and follow the orders of whoever talks at them with a semblance of authority. Although more intelligent snowmen aren\u2019t uncommon \u2014 especially if they happen to host the soul of a deceased dad for some reason \u2014 something about your brain being nothing but clumped-up ice crystals guarantees the average snowman isn\u2019t exactly the brightest light on the Christmas tree.<br /> <br /> Assuming evil sorcery isn\u2019t involved, snowpeople are as good and evil as ordinary people. Festive magic, with its innate and cheerful nature, offers snowmen the opportunity to enjoy the holidays in all their innocent splendor. Whether unbound snowpeople use it the have snowball fight in the town\u2019s square, or to be comically ineffective minions, it\u2019s purely up to them.<br /> <br /> <b>Goals</b><br /> The goals of snowmen vary from one lump of sentient snow to another, but the most important is always to preserve their bodies and protect their accessories. More powerful beings sometimes create legions of snowmen to act as their agents, but when the creatures aren\u2019t magically bound into service, their attitude resembles that of a loyal platoon, eager for success if not always effective.<br /> <br /> <b>Story Hooks</b><br /> \u2022 [REDACTED]<br /> \u2022 [REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <b>System</b><br /> Fragile yet stubborn beings, snowmen have the following average traits:<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Close Combat 2, Integrity 1, Survival 4<br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Intellect 1, Cunning 2, Resolve 3; Might 3, Dexterity 1, Stamina 3; Presence 3, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <b>Health: </b>7<br /> <br /> <b>Special Rules</b><br /> <b>Heavy amounts of snow: </b>Most snowmen are Scale 1 creatures, but bigger ones reach Scale 2 for all rolls in the Physical Arena.<br /> <br /> <b>Join the pile: </b>Multiple snowmen can join together in a single form, a last resort measure which nevertheless can overturn the outcome of a fight in a matter of seconds. As an ordinary action, a snowman can rush against another of their kin, gifting the latter their Health and merging their consciousness together. For every three snowmen fused into the same body, the Scale of their shared form rises by 1 for all Physical rolls.<br /> <br /> <b>I\u2019m melting!: </b>Given what they\u2019re made of, snowmen need a cold environment to survive. Heat sources such as strong lights or a warm fireplace impose an \u201cI\u2019m melting!\u201d Field on snowmen, causing them to lose 1 Health each round. Fire attacks also gain the Deadly tag against snowmen.<br /> <br /> <b>Plow it back: </b>It\u2019s easy to put yourself back together when the matter giving substance to your body also covers the whole neighborhood. As long as they move on snow, snowmen regain 1 Health each round. Even when reduced to 0, without the use of a Cinematic, defeated snowmen reform in the following scene. This rule deactivates whenever the <i>I\u2019m melting! </i>special rule applies.<br /> <br /> <b>Got your nose: </b>Should a character steal a snowman\u2019s carrot nose, the creature suffers a level 3 Complication on all rolls until they get their vegetable appendage back. Other snowmen present in the scene who witness this crime gain the Panicked Condition. The Attitude of all snowmen against the character and their companions starts at \u201cNegative Attitude 4\u201d for the rest of the story, since the group has made itself a hated enemy of all snowkind.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 11-11-2021, 08:27 AM"